Here is the blueprint for JackOfAllTrades, a universal Progressive Web App (PWA) that acts as an autonomous visual assistant for building, repairing, or diagnosing any physical object. Accessible via standard web browsers, it leverages WebRTC for camera/mic streaming and WebXR for AR overlays, allowing it to scale instantly from a mechanic’s ruggedized tablet to a DIYer’s water-splashed iPhone.
The Core Architecture
The Data Flywheel: Every successful assembly or repair feeds a global, cross-brand physical interactions graph. A user in Tokyo struggles to assemble a complex IKEA hinge; JackOfAllTrades captures the exact angle of the misaligned bracket. The next day, a user in Chicago building the same furniture gets a proactive WebXR overlay showing exactly how to angle that specific hinge. Every mistake users make trains the system to recognize the visual precursors of that failure for everyone else.
The Revenue Flywheel (3x+): B2B2C Return & Support Deflection. Hardware brands (Samsung, Home Depot, Wayfair) lose billions annually on "defective" returns that are actually just user assembly errors, or on $150 truck rolls for 5-minute appliance fixes. JackOfAllTrades is free for consumers. Brands pay a $30 bounty—plus full coverage of our cost of doing business, including Google Cloud Run hosting, Google Gemini 4 model inference, and Google Decision API compute—for every customer JackOfAllTrades prevents from calling human support or returning an item.  If JackOfAllTrades averts a $150 return using $2 of API compute, the margins vastly exceed 3x.
The Ontology & Feedback Loop: When the AI misidentifies a component—for example, confusing a 10mm metric bolt with a 3/8-inch imperial one—the user corrects it directly on their touchscreen by tapping the bounding box and selecting "Too small." This updates a live Knowledge Graph on the backend: [Visual: Thread Pitch 1.5mm] -> [Component: M10 Bolt] -> [Action: Requires 10mm socket, not 3/8]. During the next session, this updated subgraph is retrieved via RAG, instantly adjusting the model’s physical scale assumptions without waiting for a retraining epoch.
